# Every claim filed as a point, beside what it says would narrow it. One row per point claim
# anywhere in a document, `violates` where the answer is anything but `notApplicable`.
#
# A point has nothing to narrow
#   The rule: a point value files narrowsWhen as notApplicable, having no range. A figure with no
#   width has nothing to tighten, so any other answer is a sentence that cannot be acted on: a
#   paste from a neighbouring claim, or a claim filed at the wrong width.
#
# `unmeasured` is a violation too
#   A test for a stated narrowing cannot say so. Testing for a narrowing sentence only, a point
#   value answering "nobody has said what would narrow this" passes. But that answer presupposes
#   there is something to narrow: on a point the question is not unanswered, it is inapplicable,
#   and those are different facts.
#
# The stricter of the two readings
#   The roster sentence is why: it says the claim files notApplicable, not merely that it files
#   no condition. Every point claim in this corpus does. What would refute the strictness is a
#   point value with an honest reason to answer otherwise; `derived` would be the candidate, and
#   `tests/state_coverage.rs` has already ruled it incoherent for a narrowing, which leaves the
#   strict form standing.
#
# Written against `pm.claim`, not against demands
#   Over `layer.demand_*` this rule would be vacuous. `narrowsWhen` is on `Claim` and claims are
#   everywhere, but reach a claim's width only from the table of the thing it describes and the
#   rule can only be written against demands, no one of which is a point value in this corpus.
#   It then examines nothing and says so, loudly, which is what the coverage table is for.
#   Against `pm.claim` it examines every point claim in every document.
-- pm:Claim/pm:narrowsWhen on any pm:Claim where low = high.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT c.filing, c.layer,
           c.narrows_absent IS DISTINCT FROM 'notApplicable' AS violates,
           format('%s claim %s: %s exactly, and it still answers %s', c.owns, c.seq, c.mode,
                  coalesce(c.narrows_kind::text, 'absent: ' || c.narrows_absent)) AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(epistemics/point_claims.sqlc)
    ) c
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'narrows_a_point_value'
